  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Calculate $F\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ where $F(x)={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{x}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t.$",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =2(1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
